  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Strengthening the social contract through socio-economic infrastructure - IOM component</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Overall objective&lt;/strong&gt;: to strengthen resilience capacity and improve livelihoods of communities in liberated areas through integrated climate-adaptive socio-economic infrastructure, productive and self-sustaining livelihood investment, and social contract-strengthening initiatives.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Specific objective 1:&lt;/strong&gt; Infrastructure &amp; service delivery - foster reconciliation and trust between citizens and government institutions in recovered areas through the gender responsive, inclusive and participatory (re-) establishment of basic services and socio-economic infrastructure; &lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Specific objective 2&lt;/strong&gt;:Climate-resilient livelihoods &amp;amp; environmental peacebuilding - enable sustainable livelihood-creation in climate-resilient value chains, while ensuring natural resources are collaboratively managed between communities through inclusive governance mechanisms; &lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Specific objective 3&lt;/strong&gt;:Social contract strengthening and conflict-sensitive governance for sustainable peace - enhance locally driven governance structures by strengthening women&#xbf;s peacebuilding roles and networks and fostering inclusive decision-making processes. &lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</narrative>
  </description>
